d:82:**Note:** if you created your environment with ```pvbatch``` and you instead just do ```pip install``` (without the ```python3 -m```) then this will run your system's ```pip``` and attempt to install to the base environment (which defeats the purpose of creating this virtual environment).\nTopoPilot2Library/README.md:91:model with `topopilot.config.set_llm(...)`; the verifier can be selected\nTopoPilot2Library/README.md:95:from topopilot.api import LLM\nTopoPilot2Library/README.md:96:from topopilot.config import set_llm, set_verifier_llm\nTopoPilot2Library/README.md:148:If you used a Python virtual environment and used ```python3``` as your base, you may encounter the following error from ```pvbatch```:\nTopoPilot2Library/README.md:150:```/usr/bin/pvbatch: Error while finding module specification for 'topopilot.ui.client' (ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'topopilot')```\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a04aab-f833-7d61-ad07-a89690c1dd11"}}}
